From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: mediatek: mt6789: size pull_type to all 222 pins

mt6789_pull_type[] had 188 entries but the SoC data describes 222 pins
(GPIO188-221 are virtual EINT pins). mtk_pinconf_bias_{set,get}_combo()
indexes it by pin number, so bias get/set on those pins (debugfs
pinconf-pins, gpiod bias requests) read past the array. Size it from
mtk_pins_mt6789; the extra entries are zero.

---
diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6789.c b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6789.c
index b71f6b48b..011ee97ea 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6789.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6789.c
@@ -1133,7 +1133,7 @@ static const struct mtk_pin_field_calc mt6789_pin_rsel_range[] = {
 	PIN_FIELD_BASE(149, 149, 6, 0x0130, 0x10, 21, 3),
 };
 
-static const unsigned int mt6789_pull_type[] = {
+static const unsigned int mt6789_pull_type[ARRAY_SIZE(mtk_pins_mt6789)] = {
 	1 /* 0 */, 1 /* 1 */, 1 /* 2 */, 1 /* 3 */, 1 /* 4 */,
 	1 /* 5 */, 1 /* 6 */, 1 /* 7 */, 1 /* 8 */, 1 /* 9 */,
 	1 /* 10 */, 1 /* 11 */, 1 /* 12 */, 1 /* 13 */, 1 /* 14 */,
